      en: "Haw Phra Kaew, once a prominent Buddhist temple in Vientiane, now serves as a renowned museum of religious art. The building was originally commissioned in 1565 by King Setthathirath to house the highly venerated Emerald Buddha, which he had brought from Chiang Mai. After residing there for over two centuries, the sacred statue was reclaimed by Siamese forces in 1779, and the temple was severely damaged during subsequent conflicts. The magnificent structure seen today is the result of an extensive reconstruction effort in the 1930s and 1940s, which carefully preserved original Lao stylistic elements."
